# Excalidraw diagrams

The `.excalidraw` file sits next to the document that embeds the picture. The design document uses `part1/langsmith-deployment.excalidraw`. The deck uses the scenes in `present/assets/`. `langsmith-deployment.excalidraw` is used in both places, so that scene is duplicated. Copy an edit onto both files before exporting. Earlier versions stay in `plans/diagrams/`.

The user opens a scene at http://localhost:8080 and exports `.excalidraw` back over the same path.

```bash
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name my-excalidraw-instance excalidraw/excalidraw:latest
```

The image listens on container port 80.

## Check the picture

After a create or edit, run `./scripts/export-diagrams.sh`, read the PNG, and fix what it shows. Repeat until the picture is clean. The JSON stays the file to edit.

The script writes the PNG beside the scene. A scene in `part1/` or `present/` is also copied into `deliverables/`. A scene under `plans/` is not.

The exporter draws text in the hand-drawn font, not Helvetica. Fix overlap and clipping. Do not restyle the scene to match that font.

## Revisions

- Patch by stable element `id`. Do not regenerate a scene the user has saved.
- A new version is a new file (`name-v2.excalidraw`). Leave the previous file untouched.
- Do not write the version into the frame name or any other canvas text.

## Layout

Use Helvetica (`fontFamily` 2). Keep each column only as wide as its longest line. Stack lists one item per line.

- Purpose note above each agent: fill `#e7f5ff`, `strokeWidth` 0, no arrow.
- Card under the step: `prompt` and the filename on one line, then `tools`, then `output`. One tool or state field per line. `none` is `#868e96`.
- Output rows sit on `#b2f2bb`.
- Excalidraw has no bold. Draw a label twice, 0.7px apart.
- A branch is a `diamond` with yes and no arrows, not a flat list.
- Something that is not a step (a sample repo) has `frameId` null and no arrows.
- Mission text is a top callout: fill `#fff4e6`, roughness 0, left bar `#e8590c`.

## Legend

Swatches, not a sentence: `#a5d8ff` agent, `#ffec99` placeholder, `#ffd8a8` human gate, `#e9ecef` start and end, `#b2f2bb` output.

## Ids

Use readable ids (`node-diff`, `card-diff`, `text-card-diff-tool-1`, `diamond-ready`). Keep arrow bindings and `boundElements` in sync. Give new elements the next fractional `index` (`a0`…`az`, then `b00`).
